```java
import java.io.*;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        StateObject state = loadStateFromFile("state.ser");

        if (state != null) {
            System.out.println("State loaded successfully!");
            // Use the state object here...
        } else {
            System.out.println("Failed to load state from file.");
        }
    }

    private static StateObject loadStateFromFile(String filename) {
        ObjectInputStream inputStream = null;

        try {
            FileInputStream fileIn = new FileInputStream(filename);
            inputStream = new ObjectInputStream(fileIn);

            return (StateObject)inputStream.readObject();
        } catch (IOException | ClassNotFoundException e) {
            System.err.println("Failed to deserialize object from " + filename);
            e.printStackTrace();
        } finally {
            if (inputStream != null) {
                try {
                    inputStream.close();
                } catch (IOException e) {
                    e.printStackTrace();
                }
            }
        }

        return null;
    }
}
```
This Java program safely loads a StateObject from a file named "state.ser", handling any exceptions that may occur during deserialization and ensuring the ObjectInputStream is closed properly, even if an exception occurs during deserialization. 

