```java
@Service
public class ResourceManagementService {
    private final CacheManager cacheManager; // Assume you have a cache manager here
    private final MessageBrokerClient messageBrokerClient; // Assume you have a client for RabbitMQ or Kafka here
    private final VersionControlService versionControlService; // Assume you have a service for rate limiting and monitoring here

    public Resource createResource(Resource resource) {
        cacheManager.saveToCache(resource);
        messageBrokerClient.publish("new_resource", resource);
        versionControlService.incrementRateLimit();

        // handle exceptions, log errors, etc.
    }

    public Resource getResource(String id) {
        return cacheManager.getFromCache(id).orElseGet(() -> {
            Resource resource = // Get from the database or external service here
            cacheManager.saveToCache(resource);
            return resource;
        });

        // handle exceptions, log errors, etc.
    }

    public void updateResource(String id, Resource updated) {
        Resource current = getResource(id);

        if (current == null) throw new NotFoundException();

        try {
            resourceDao.update(updated); // Assume you have a DAO for database operations here

            versionControlService.incrementRateLimit();
            messageBrokerClient.publish("resource_updated", updated);
            cacheManager.saveToCache(updated);
        } catch (OptimisticLockingFailureException e) {
            // handle optimistic lock exception, retry after some time, etc.
        } 

        // handle exceptions, log errors, etc.
    }

    public void deleteResource(String id) {
        resourceDao.deleteById(id);
        cacheManager.invalidateCacheEntry(id);
        versionControlService.incrementRateLimit();

        // handle exceptions, log errors, etc.
    }
}
```
2. **Cache Manager** - This service manages the Redis cache and handles eviction policies.
3. **Message Broker Client** - This service communicates with Kafka or RabbitMQ for managing messages. 
