['This is quite a complex task and writing complete code for it here would be impractical due to its length, complexity and specific requirements. However, I can provide you with a basic skeleton for such a logging framework in C. 

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <time.h>
#include <pthread.h>

// Define Log Levels
typedef enum {DEBUG, INFO, WARNING, ERROR} log_level;

// Declare Global Mutex for Thread Safety 
pthread_mutex_t lock = PTHREAD_MUTEX_INITIALIZER;

void log_message(log_level level, const char* message) {
    pthread_mutex_lock(&lock); // Lock Mutex to Ensure Atomicity

    time_t t = time(NULL);  // Get Current Time
    struct tm *tm = localtime(&t);  // Convert Time Structure

    char time_str[64];  // String to Hold Formatted Time
    strftime(time_str, sizeof(time_str), "%c", tm);  // Format Current Time

    FILE *logfile = fopen("application.log","a");  // Open Log File in Append Mode
    char loglevel[20];  

    switch (level) {  // Determine Log Level
        case DEBUG: strcpy(loglevel, "DEBUG"); break;
        case INFO: strcpy(loglevel, "INFO"); break;
        case WARNING: strcpy(loglevel, "WARNING"); break;
        case ERROR: strcpy(loglevel, "ERROR"); break;
    }  

    // Log Message to File 
    fprintf(logfile,"[%s] [%s]: %s\n", time_str, loglevel, message);

    fclose(logfile);  // Close File

    pthread_mutex_unlock(&lock);  // Unlock Mutex after Operation
}
```
Please note that this code only covers a basic logging framework. To create an extensive and robust system as you requested, you would need to significantly extend it, including the addition of error handling for failed log writes or configuration parsing errors, dynamic enabling/disabling of logging at runtime, self-healing mechanisms for distributed logging nodes, visualization tools, exporting logs to analytics platforms, etc. Also remember that system-level dependencies such as third-party components can greatly affect the performance and reliability of your logging framework, so considerations for these factors should be taken into account in the design phase.
