["This task seems like an extensive software system design problem which can't be fully solved in a few code blocks here due to the complexity involved. However, I can help you with creating classes for each challenge and show how they could interact with each other.

Here is an example of a class implementing dynamic rate-limiting strategy:

```java
public class RateLimiter {
    private final Map<String, Queue<Long>> rateLimits;

    public RateLimiter() {
        this.rateLimits = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
    }

    public void acquire(String api) throws InterruptedException {
        if (!this.rateLimits.containsKey(api)) {
            synchronized (this) {
                if (!this.rateLimits.containsKey(api)) {
                    this.rateLimits.put(api, new ConcurrentLinkedQueue<>());
                }
            }
        }

        Queue<Long> queue = rateLimits.get(api);
        long currentTime = System.currentTimeMillis();

        while (!queue.isEmpty() && currentTime - queue.peek() >= 1000) { // 1 second interval for example
            queue.remove();
        }

        if (queue.size() >= getRateLimit(api)) {
            Thread.sleep(1000); // sleep for a second before retrying
            acquire(api);
        } else {
