['Creating a full-featured library in C for such requirements would be quite complex and extensive. However, here's an example of how you could create a `CreateParameterizedSQLCommand` function to execute parameterized SQL commands using ADO.NET in C#:

```csharp
using System;
using System.Data;
using System.Data.SqlClient;

public class SqlHelper
{
    private const int CommandTimeout = 30; // Adjust this value as per your requirement

    public static IDataReader ExecuteParameterizedSQLCommand(string connectionString, string sqlQuery, params object[] parameters)
    {
        if (connectionString == null) throw new ArgumentNullException("connectionString");
        if (sqlQuery == null) throw new ArgumentNullException("sqlQuery");

        using (var conn = new SqlConnection(connectionString))
        {
            conn.Open();

            using (var command = conn.CreateCommand())
            {
                command.CommandText = sqlQuery;
                command.CommandTimeout = CommandTimeout;

                for (int i = 0; i < parameters.Length; ++i)
                {
                    var parameter = new SqlParameter();
                    parameter.Value = parameters[i] ?? DBNull.Value;
                    command.Parameters.Add(parameter);
                }

                return command.ExecuteReader(CommandBehavior.CloseConnection);
            }
        }
    }
}
```
In this code, `CreateParameterizedSQLCommand` is a static method that accepts three arguments: `connectionString` (the connection string for the SQL database), `sqlQuery` (the parameterized SQL command to be executed), and `parameters` (an array of parameters for the SQL command). It returns an IDataReader which can be used to read the result set.

This code is secure against SQL injection because it uses parameterized queries, a feature provided by ADO.NET that automatically escapes special characters in query values to prevent them from interfering with the structure of the query itself. This method also handles large result sets efficiently as the data is returned one row at a time, reducing memory usage.
']

