        va_list args;
        va_start(args, format);

        char buffer[MAX_BUFFER];
        vsnprintf(buffer, MAX_BUFFER, format, args);

        syslog(LOG_ERR | LOG_USER, "%s", buffer);
        closelog();

        va_end(args);
    }
}
```
This function logs an error message if the condition is true. The variadic arguments are used to format a string which is then logged using syslog with priority level LOG_ERR. Please note that you would want to wrap this in a try-catch block and ensure proper resource management depending on your use case and system requirements.
