In this example, we're using a Spring Cloud Feign client to interact with an external API. This service will automatically be registered in your Eureka server (if you have one) and Ribbon is used for load balancing and fault tolerance. 

For caching, you could use Spring Boot Cache:
```java
import org.springframework.cache.annotation.Cacheable;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Service;

@Service
public class PokemonTypeService {
    private final PokemonApi pokemonApi;

    public PokemonTypeService(PokemonApi pokemonApi) {
        this.pokemonApi = pokemonApi;
    }

    @Cacheable("pokemons")
    public Mono<PokemonTypes> getPokemonTypes(String id){
        return pokemonApi.getPokemonTypes(id);
    }
}
```
In this case, the `@Cacheable` annotation is used to cache the results of our method in a distributed cache (Redis for example). If the same request comes again within the cache's configured timeout period, it will return the cached result instead of calling the API. 

To handle errors and fallbacks, you could use Spring Cloud Circuit Breaker:
```java
import org.springframework.cloud.client.circuitbreaker.CircuitBreakerFactory;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Service;

@Service
public class PokemonTypeService {
    private final PokemonApi pokemonApi;
    private final CircuitBreakerFactory circuitBreakerFactory;

    public PokemonTypeService(PokemonApi pokemonApi, CircuitBreakerFactory circuitBreakerFactory) {
        this.pokemonApi = pokemonApi;
        this.circuitBreakerFactory = circuitBreakerFactory;
    }

    @Cacheable("pokemons")
    public Mono<PokemonTypes> getPokemonTypes(String id){
        return circuitBreakerFactory.create("getPokemonTypes").run(() -> 
            pokemonApi.getPokemonTypes(id)
                .onErrorResume(e -> {
                    // handle error here and provide a fallback
                })
        );
    }
}
```
This uses Spring Cloud's circuit breaker to wrap our API call in case of failures, allowing it to fail fast instead of continuing to block the thread. You can also define different fallbacks for different types of exceptions.

