['Implementing a full-fledged cryptographic library with all these features is a complex task that requires deep understanding of C/C++ programming, cryptography, network communication, error handling and system management. Below I've provided a simplified example of how to implement the requested function in C++ using STL. 

For real-world usage, consider utilizing existing well-established libraries like OpenSSL or Botan. Also, keep in mind that writing secure cryptographic code is very challenging task and requires deep understanding of cryptography and security principles. It's not recommended to implement your own cryptography library unless you're doing it as a learning exercise.

```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <forward_list>
#include <string>

void insertAfterTarget(std::forward_list<std::string>& list, const std::string& target, const std::string& replacement) {
    bool found = false;
    auto prevIt = list.before_begin();
    for (auto it = list.begin(); it != list.end(); ++it) {
        if (*it == target) {
            found = true;
            list.insert_after(it, replacement);
            break;
        }
        prevIt = it;
    }

    // Target string not found - append to the end of the list
    if (!found) {
        list.insert_after(prevIt, replacement);
    }
}

int main() {
    std::forward_list<std::string> words = {"hello", "world"};

    // Target string found - insert after the first occurrence
    insertAfterTarget(words, "world", "!");  // Output: hello world !

    for (const auto& word : words) {
        std::cout << word << ' ';
    }
    std::cout << '\n';

    // Target string not found - append to the end of the list
    insertAfterTarget(words, "C++", "programming");  // Output: hello world ! programming

    for (const auto& word : words) {
        std::cout << word << ' ';
    }
    std::cout << '\n';

    return 0;
}
```
This code demonstrates how to insert a string after the first occurrence of another in a forward_list. If the target is not found, it's appended to the end of the list. The function modifies the input list directly without returning anything.
']

