['Implementing this task in detail involves several aspects including designing microservices architecture, implementing security features such as JWT tokens, MFA using TOTP and hardware security keys, integrating with third-party identity providers, managing database operations (including encryption), monitoring user activity and anomaly detection, load testing, logging and monitoring system, implementing Union-Find data structure for calculating disjoint pairs in an array, designing a multi-tenant architecture. This task is too broad to be implemented here but I can provide an example of how the Java function for union-find data structure could look like:

```java
import java.util.*;

public class UnionFind {
    private int[] parent;  // parent[i] = parent of i
    private byte[] rank;   // rank[i] = rank of subtree rooted at i (never more than 31)
    private int count;     // number of components

    public UnionFind(int n) {
        if (n < 0) throw new IllegalArgumentException();
        count = n;
        parent = new int[n];
        rank = new byte[n];
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            parent[i] = i;
            rank[i] = 0;
        }
    }

    public int count() {
        return count;
    }

    public int find(int p) {
        validate(p);
        while (p != parent[p]) {
            parent[p] = parent[parent[p]];    // path compression by halving
            p = parent[p];
        }
        return p;
    }

    public boolean connected(int p, int q) {
        return find(p) == find(q);
    }

    public void union(int p, int q) {
        int rootP = find(p);
        int rootQ = find(q);
        if (rootP == rootQ) return;
        // make root of smaller rank point to root of larger rank
        if      (rank[rootP] < rank[rootQ]) parent[rootP] = rootQ;
        else if (rank[rootP] > rank[rootQ]) parent[rootQ] = rootP;
        else {
            parent[rootQ] = rootP;
            rank[rootP]++;
        }
        count--;
    }

    // validate that p is a valid index
    private void validate(int p) {
        int n = parent.length;
        if (p < 0 || p >= n) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("index " + p + " is not between 0 and " + (n-1));  
        }
    }
}
```
This is just a basic UnionFind algorithm implementation in Java. It can be extended according to the requirements of the task. Please note that designing, implementing, testing, securing, optimizing and deploying such a system is a very complex task which requires deep understanding of many aspects including microservices architecture, security, database management, machine learning models, logging systems etc.
']

