['Implementing such an extensive system is beyond the scope of this platform but here's how you can create a simple modular Python API gateway using Flask and several other libraries like Flask-Limiter, Flask-SocketIO, Flask-HTTPAuth, Redis for caching. Please note that this code won't run as is because it needs to be integrated with third-party services, the event bus setup, backup/disaster recovery, AWS and Azure integration, machine learning model integrations, etc., which are out of scope here:

```python
from flask import Flask, request
from flask_limiter import Limiter
from flask_socketio import SocketIO, emit
from flask_httpauth import HTTPTokenAuth
from redis import Redis
import requests

app = Flask(__name__)
limiter = Limiter(app)
socketio = SocketIO(app)
auth = HTTPTokenAuth(scheme='Bearer')
redis = Redis()

@app.route('/api/<path:endpoint>', methods=['GET', 'POST'])
@auth.login_required
@limiter.limit("100/day;10/hour")
def api(endpoint):
    if request.method == 'POST':
        data = request.get_json()
        # Route the POST request to appropriate service and cache response
        response = requests.post(f'https://{endpoint}', json=data)
        redis.set(endpoint, response.text)  # Caching response
    else:
        # If cached, return cached data instead of making a new request
        if redis.exists(endpoint):
            return redis.get(endpoint)  
        else:
            response = requests.get(f'https://{endpoint}') 
            redis.set(endpoint, response.text)  # Caching response
    emit('response', response.json(), broadcast=False)

@socketio.on('connect')
def test_connect():
    emit('my response', {'data': 'Connected'})

if __name__ == '__main__':
    socketio.run(app, debug=True)
```
This is a very simplified example and would need to be built out considerably for production use. The machine learning models integration, AWS & Azure integration, backup/disaster recovery strategy, comprehensive monitoring and alerting system setup, etc., are all additional steps that would be needed beyond the code provided above. 

Also, remember this is just one aspect of API Gateway's architecture. As such it should follow other best practices such as using environment variables for sensitive data (like database credentials), properly handling errors and edge cases, testing, logging etc., which were not covered in this example.
