['Here is the code skeleton based on your instructions. This is a high-level overview of how such service can be designed, and actual implementation will vary greatly depending on specific requirements and constraints. Please adjust this code as per your need, also for each piece of functionality we are providing basic pseudo code which needs to be replaced with actual implementation.

```csharp
public class LogProcessingService : ILogProcessingService
{
    private readonly ConcurrentQueue<Log> _queue;
    private readonly AutoResetEvent _signal = new AutoResetEvent(false);

    public LogProcessingService()
    {
        _queue = new ConcurrentQueue<Log>();

        var thread = new Thread(Consume)
        {
            IsBackground = true,
            Name = "Log Processing Service Consumer"
        };
        thread.Start();
    }

    public async Task EnqueueAsync(Log item)
    {
        _queue.Enqueue(item);
        _signal.Set(); // notify the consumer
    }

    private void Consume()
    {
        while (true)
        {
            if (!_queue.TryDequeue(out var log))
            {
                _signal.WaitOne();  // wait for signal from producer
                continue;
            }

            try
            {
                HandleLog(log); // call a method to handle the log processing, validation etc.
            }
            catch (Exception ex)
            {
                // error handling and logging
            }
        }
    }

    private void HandleLog(Log log){
       // Logic for real-time data handling, reliable storage, flexible validation, resource optimization, 
       // advanced error handling and logging goes here. This code will be dependent on the actual implementation and might be complex.
       // Please refer to the detailed design in the steps above. 
    }
}
```
This is a basic asynchronous producer-consumer pattern where `EnqueueAsync` is for receiving real-time data streams, and `Consume` is the method where logs are processed. This can be extended with other patterns depending on use cases and requirements. For example, if you need to process multiple log items concurrently, you could use a parallel `foreach` loop in `Consume`.

For real-time data handling, reliable storage, flexible validation, resource optimization, advanced error handling and logging, they are complex functionalities and would require additional classes and methods that will be called from the `HandleLog` method. Please refer to each section for a detailed design of these functionalities.
