Please note that this code snippet is just to give you an idea about what your solution could look like. There are many more aspects you need to consider when designing a real-world system, like security, observability, fault tolerance etc. So please modify it as per your specific use case.

```java
import org.springframework.boot.SpringApplication;
import org.springframework.cloud.client.discovery.EnableDiscoveryClient;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.GetMapping;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.PathVariable;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.RestController;
import java.util.*;
import java.util.concurrent.ThreadLocalRandom;

@EnableDiscoveryClient
@SpringBootApplication
public class RngServiceApplication {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        SpringApplication.run(RngServiceApplication.class, args);
    }
}

@RestController
class RandomNumberGeneratorController {

    @GetMapping("/random/{type}/{bound}")
    Map<String, Object> random(@PathVariable String type, @PathVariable int bound) {
        double random = 0;
        switch (type) {
            case "uniform":
                random = ThreadLocalRandom.current().nextDouble(bound);
                break;
            case "gaussian":
                random = ThreadLocalRandom.current().nextGaussian();
                break;
            case "exponential":
                random = -Math.log(1 - ThreadLocalRandom.current().nextDouble()) / bound;
                break;
        }

        return Collections.singletonMap("number", random);
    }
}
```
This Java application creates a RESTful service which can generate different types of random numbers. You can customize it further to support custom distribution types and integrate with external services as per your requirements. 

